  </p>
  <h1>The D.E.A.L. Framework: Scale Revenue Without Adding People</h1>
  <p class="lead">Most growth companies have the same problem: sales is moving — but only because someone is running faster. That's not a system. That's a crisis waiting to happen.</p>

  <div class="section" style="background:#f8f8f8; padding:1.5rem; border-radius:4px; margin-bottom:2rem;">
    <p style="margin:0; font-size:0.95rem;"><strong>Key numbers:</strong> According to Salesforce research, 67% of sales reps don't expect to hit quota. The primary cause isn't effort — it's the absence of a repeatable system. The D.E.A.L. Framework addresses exactly that.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <p>Picture this: You're leading a growth company, the numbers are ticking upwards, but sales still feel like spinning plates. Every win is because someone — probably you — is running faster, juggling more, basically being a hero. That's not a system. It's a crisis waiting to happen.</p>
    <p>This is exactly why I built the D.E.A.L. Framework. A simple but powerful approach to build a revenue system that scales cleanly — without the need to add headcount or rely on miracle workers.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>D — Data</h2>
    <p>Clean data is your fuel. If your CRM is a graveyard of outdated contact info and missed signals, you're driving blind.</p>
    <p><strong>Mini-exercise:</strong> Pick one sales rep or customer segment. Audit their last 10 deals in your CRM. How many have missing fields or outdated info? Set a rule: if data isn't updated within one week, it's flagged for review before you chase new leads.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>E — Execution</h2>
    <p>A repeatable, documented sales process is your revenue backbone. No more relying on the charisma or "superstar" powers of individuals.</p>
    <p><strong>Mini-exercise:</strong> Write down your current sales stages as simply as possible. Next, identify one critical handoff point where deals typically stall. What's the exact action required? Make this your immediate focus for streamlining.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>A — Augmentation</h2>
    <p>Toggle Tax is real: salespeople lose heaps of time switching between tools and screens. AI-augmented selling isn't science fiction — it's the productivity hack you should already be using.</p>
    <p><strong>Mini-exercise:</strong> Track how many apps your sales team toggles between in a day. Can you consolidate or automate 10% of those actions with AI-based tools? Even simple email drafting, note-taking, or qualification scoring can save serious time.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>L — Leadership</h2>
    <p>Strong systems don't build themselves. Coaching founders and sales leaders to lead with clarity and consistency is the multiplier that turns frameworks into results.</p>
    <p><strong>Mini-exercise:</strong> Schedule a short weekly coaching moment — 15 minutes max — with your sales lead or key founder. Focus on what system tweak they experimented with that week and what the result was.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2>The truth about scaling sales</h2>
    <p>Scaling sales doesn't require more people — it requires better systems and smarter leadership. The D.E.A.L. Framework will get you there.</p>
